+===================================================================
+=== SECTION 1: ARCHITECTURAL OVERVIEW & BROWSER COMPATIBILITY   ===
+===================================================================
+
+Project Architecture:
+  Languages: TypeScript 5.4, JavaScript ES2022
+  Framework: Vanilla TypeScript/JS with Material Design CSS
+  Manifest Version: Manifest V3 across all supported browsers
+  Supported Browsers:
+    1. Google Chrome & Chromium-based browsers (Edge, Brave, Opera)
+       - Manifest: browser/chrome/manifest.json (MV3, background.service_worker)
+       - Shortcut Config URL: chrome://extensions/shortcuts or edge://extensions/shortcuts
+       - Shortcut Limits: Max 4 commands with suggested_key; unlimited configurable commands
+    2. Mozilla Firefox (Gecko >= 109.0)
+       - Manifest: browser/firefox/manifest.json (MV3, background.scripts module)
+       - Shortcut Config URL: about:addons -> Manage Extension Shortcuts
+       - Shortcut Limits: Max 4 commands with suggested_key; unlimited configurable commands
+    3. Apple Safari (macOS / iPadOS / iOS)
+       - Manifest: browser/safari/manifest.json (MV3, background.service_worker)
+       - Shortcut Config: Safari Settings -> Extensions -> Shortcuts
+       - Specifics: Safari does not support chrome.alarms or chrome.downloads; uses fallback handlers
+
+Command API Strategy:
+  - Up to 4 high-priority commands assigned suggested_key defaults (including _execute_action).
+  - All eligible popup actions declared in manifest.json under 'commands' with unique command IDs and descriptions.
+  - Users can configure any command natively in their browser's shortcut manager.
+  - Centralized command dispatcher in background service worker decoupled from popup lifecycle.
+  - Shared action handler service used by both popup UI event listeners and background command dispatcher.
+
